      "body": "## Summary\n- Follow-up to #54867 / #58055 / #59050 (test-tethering check): shrinks the allowlist by 10 more entries by wiring CPU-safe tests into one new CPU job in `misc.yaml`, `cpu-distributed-platforms-cli` (`:computer: (CPU) Distributed, Platforms, CLI`, 20 min). It installs nothing at runtime and just runs `pytest` on the prebuilt `image-build-cpu` image, so it is unaffected by the dependency-locking disablements in #63608 / #63609. The whole set runs in well under a minute, so one job avoids paying a second pod startup.\n  - Distributed (7): `test_expert_placement.py`, `test_file_store.py`, `test_kvlayout.py`, `test_kv_cache_events.py`, `test_mq_connect_ip.py`, `test_pipeline_partition.py`, `aux_output_connector/test_store.py` (added by #45635).\n  - Platforms / CLI / tools (3): `platforms/test_cpu.py` (run with an explicit `VLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=cpu`), `entrypoints/cli/test_serve.py` (added by #53124), `tools/test_config_validator.py` (`tools/` is baked into the CPU test image, `Dockerfile.cpu`).\n  - `source_file_dependencies` lists the modules the tests actually import (checked against each test's `vllm`/`tools` imports), not just their own directories: `vllm/distributed/`, `vllm/config/`, `vllm/platforms/`, `vllm/entrypoints/{cli,launchers}/`, `vllm/logger.py`, `vllm/utils/network_utils.py`, `expert_map_manager.py`, `vllm/v1/{core/sched/output.py,outputs.py,worker/gpu/async_utils.py}` and `tools/pre_commit/validate_config.py`.\n- Despite the old \"multi-GPU\" wording on the `test_expert_placement.py` allowlist entry, none of the 10 files need a GPU: all pass with every GPU hidden.\n- Rebased over #63608 / #63609, which commented out neighbouring blocks in `misc.yaml` and re-added many allowlist entries; the remaining \"CI jobs disabled pending locked ... installation\" entries are untouched.\n\n## Test plan\n- `python tools/pre_commit/check_test_tethering.py --all`: exit 0, no new gaps.\n- All 10 files run with `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES`/`HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES`/`ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES` empty: 123 passed, 0 skipped across 9 files (7 distributed + `test_serve` + `test_config_validator`), plus `platforms/test_cpu.py` run separately under `VLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=cpu`, which also passes. (Local env is a ROCm build, so this approximates but is not the real CPU image; the new CPU jobs are the real check.)\n- pre-commit hooks that apply to the changed files (yaml, check-test-tethering, signoff, etc.) pass.\n\nAI assistance was used (Claude Code) to check which allowlisted tests are CPU-safe, wire the CI jobs and rebase over the dependency-disablement PRs. All changes reviewed and tested locally per AGENTS.md before opening.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
